# Domain invariants

## Content hierarchy

`Universe` → `Arc` → `Story` (`short_story` | `chapters` | `comic`) → chapters/blocks or `comic_pages`.

- Story `universe_id` / `arc_id` must be owned by the caller (universe owner). Enforce in API domain (`scope`) + existing DB triggers.
- `feed_display_mode`: `preview` | `cover`.

## Do not merge these systems

| System | Tables / routes | Purpose |
|--------|-----------------|---------|
| Avisos | `notification_subscriptions`, `notifications` | Subscribe to author/universe for new stories |
| Activity | `activity_notifications` | Mentions, comments, likes, collection saves |
| Follows | `universe_follows` | Feed personalization only |
| Library | likes + `library_collections*` | Shelves / collections |

Separate SSE streams, hooks (`useNotificationInbox` vs `useActivityNotificationInbox`), and UI copy.

## Authz

App-layer in Rust only. Public read / authenticated write per `apps/api/docs/AUTHZ.md` — verify against code if docs look stale.
